    "title": "Where to watch Colorado vs Illinois women's basketball in March Madness",
    "text": "March 21, 2026, 1:01 p.m. MTColorado women's basketball is back in the NCAA Tournament for the fourth time in five years and, after being named a No. 10 seed, has a winnable first-round game. The Buffaloes will take on the No. 7 seed Illinois Fighting Illini.CU is 22-11 overall (11-7 Big 12) after another successful regular season, while the Illini are 21-11 overall (9-9 Big Ten). Colorado lost in the semifinals of the Big 12 Tournament to the eventual champion, West Virginia. Illinois lost to Iowa in the Big Ten Tournament quarterfinals.The Buffs are led by head coach JR Payne and by three players averaging double figures: Jade Masogayo, Zyanna Walker and Desiree Wooten.Colorado will need to slow down the solid Illinois offense that features First Team All-Big Ten selection Berry Wallace, who is averaging 18.4 points per game.The winner of Saturday's game will face either No. 2 Vanderbilt or No. 15 High Point in the second round. Here's everything you need to know to tune in for the matchup between the Buffaloes and the Fighting Illini.Colorado women's basketball vs. Illinois: TV channel, tip timeDate: Saturday, March 21TV Channel: ESPN2Start Time: 9:30 p.m. ET, 7:30 p.m. MTNo. 7 Illinois vs. No. 10 Colorado will tip off at 7:30 p.m. MT on Saturday, March 21, from Vanderbilt's Memorial Gym in Nashville, Tennessee.Where to stream Colorado vs. IllinoisColorado-Illinois will be available to stream on the ESPN app (with a TV provider login) and on Fubo, which offers a free trial to new subscribers.Watch Colorado vs. Illinois in the NCAA Tournament on ESPN2Follow Charlie Strella on X (formerly Twitter), Threads and Instagram.Contact/Follow us @BuffaloesWire on X (formerly Twitter) and like our page on Facebook for ongoing coverage of Colorado news, notes and opinions.Our team of savvy editors independently handpicks all recommendations. If you purchase through our links, the USA TODAY Network may earn a commission. Prices were accurate at the time of publication but may change.",
